<title>USA: Tables of emerging market investment -- World Bank.</title>
<headline>Tables of emerging market investment -- World Bank.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The World Bank on Sunday issued its report on global development finance. The following table shows net private capital flows to developing countries by country group (billions of U.S. dollars):</p>
<p>				    1996   1995   1994</p>
<p> All Developing Countries  243.8  184.2  161.3</p>
<p> Sub-Saharan Africa	   11.8    9.1    5.2</p>
<p> East Asia/Pacific	   108.7   84.1   71.0</p>
<p> South Asia		     10.7    5.2    8.5</p>
<p> Europe/Central Asia	  31.2   30.1   17.2</p>
<p> Latin America/Caribbean    74.3   54.3   53.6</p>
<p> Mideast/North Africa	  6.9    1.4    5.8</p>
<p>Top 12 country destinations (billions of U.S. dollars):</p>
<p>				    1996   1995   1994</p>
<p> China			    52.0   44.3   44.4</p>
<p> Mexico			   28.1   13.1   20.7</p>
<p> Brazil			   14.7   19.1   12.2</p>
<p> Malaysia			 16.0   11.9    8.9</p>
<p> Indonesia			17.9   11.6    7.7</p>
<p> Thailand			 13.3    9.1    4.8</p>
<p> Argentina			11.3    7.2    7.6</p>
<p> India			     8.0    3.6    6.4</p>
<p> Russia			    3.6    1.1    0.3</p>
<p> Turkey			    4.7    2.0    1.6</p>
<p> Chile			     4.6    4.2    4.3</p>
<p> Hungary			   2.5    7.8    2.8</p>
<p>Percentage of share of</p>
<p> top twelve countries	 72.5   73.3   75.4</p>
<p>Note: 1996 data is preliminary. Ranking of the top 12 country destinations is based on cumulative 1990-95 private capital inflows received. Private flows include commercial bank loans guaranteed by export credit agencies.</p>
</text>
